Body:
@kanagawa6 

Until OpenCode Go's openapi compatibility supports native FIM, the only workaround to implement your own translation proxy between zed's request and OpenCode Go.

I've implemented a minimal lightweight proxy, repo: [claytonchew/zed-opencode-fim-proxy](https://github.com/claytonchew/zed-opencode-fim-proxy) – it works but not as good as native FIM should be.

```
The PR comment says plain @ai-sdk/google “rewrites these,” but the PR does not implement the same rewrite.
@ai-sdk/google converts:
{ "type": ["number", "string"] }
into:
{
  "anyOf": [
    { "type": "number" },
    { "type": "string" }
  ]
}
The PR converts it into:
{ "type": "number" }
It simply keeps the first non-null type, losing "string".
```

@dreamorosi I think this should fix it:
https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/commit/e2527db3c7fec561572135f0dddebca5871ba79e

Going to release later today, im marking this issue as closed since i think this should resolve it, if not we will reopen.
